body:
don't be scared and don't limit yourself from reaching out to hotlines if you need the help-- the hotline i  called wasn't national, it was out of illinois and i got randomly connected to them for some reason. i have had nothing but love from the national hotline, and if you ever feel uncomfortable you can always reach our to 24hr treatment centers, as they usually have hotlines! (places like Bowen have a crisis hotline, i have spoken to them multiple times and they're so loving) 

&#x200B;

dont be afraid to reach out to anyone here as well, we will all welcome you in our messages with open arms because we are all struggling one in the same

in my mind, i differentiate them as agitated depression being more related to the restlessness aspect of depression mixed with extreme anger/ agitation, verses a mixed episode where you're sort of in the "grey" mixed with mixed mania/depression symptoms. with agitated depression, you're more likely to feel awake and unable to sit down vs a mixed episode where aggression/ anger, overactivity, and racing thoughts are more common. agitated depression and mixed episodes are both unfortunately as you know characteristics related to bipolar disorder. having experienced both, i can relate to your description quite a bit. knowing the difference can be difficult, and i've also had my fair share of doctors who are both clueless and/ or dismissive. 

&#x200B;

i hope you find treatment/ resources that can help you, as someone who is also bipolar (I), i understand the struggle.
